        "original_id": "269cfa6b-9423-5486-875b-26a6236081c5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lakshmibai, Rani of Jhansi\n- Places: Rani Jhansi Marine National Park, Middle Button Island National Park, North Button, South Button, Jhansi, Uttar Pradesh, South Andaman Island, North India\n- Topics: Commemoration, national parks\n\nFacts:\n- Lakshmibai, the Rani of Jhansi, was born on 19 November 1828 and died on 18 June 1858.\n- Lakshmibai was the queen of the princely state of Jhansi in North India, in the area now in Jhansi district, Uttar Pradesh, India.\n- Rani Jhansi Marine National Park commemorates Lakshmibai, the Rani of Jhansi.\n- Middle Button Island National Park, together with the neighbouring islands of North Button and South Button, forms part of Rani Jhansi Marine National Park off the coast of South Andaman Island.",
